====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|metal in horse's mouth}} A piece of metal placed in a horse's mouth and connected to the reins to direct the animal.
#: {{ux|en|A horse hates having a '''bit''' put in its mouth.}}
# A [[rotary]] [[cut]]ting [[tool]] fitted to a [[drill]], used to [[bore]] [[hole]]s.
# {{lb|en|dated|British}} A coin of a specified value.
#: {{ux|en|a threepenny '''bit'''}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|Canada}} A ten-[[cent]] piece, [[dime]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1941|author=w:Emily Carr|title=w:Klee Wyck|url=http://www.gutenberg.net.au/ebooks01/0100131h.html|chapter=10
|passage=The smallest coin we had in Canada in early days was a dime, worth ten cents. The Indians called this coin "a '''Bit'''". Our next coin, double in buying power and in size, was a twenty-five cent piece and this the Indians called "Two Bits".}}
# {{lb|en|now|US}} A unit of currency or coin in the Americas worth a fraction of a Spanish dollar; now specifically, an eighth of a US [[dollar]].
#: {{ux|en|A quarter is two '''bits'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1789|author=w:Olaudah Equiano|title=The Interesting Narrative|volume=I|chapter=6
|passage=I trusted to the Lord to be with me; and at one of our trips to St. Eustatia, a Dutch island, I bought a glass tumbler with my half '''bit''', and when I came to Montserrat I sold it for a '''bit''', or sixpence.}}
#* {{RQ:Pynchon Crying Lot|page=16|passage=He left after shaking her down for four '''bits''' for carrying the bags.}}
# {{senseid|en|silver coin}} {{lb|en|historical|US}} In the southern and southwestern states, a small silver coin (such as the [[real]]) formerly current; commonly, one worth about 12½ cents; also, the sum of 12½ cents.
# A [[small]] [[amount]] of something.
#: {{ux|en|There were '''bits''' of paper all over the floor.}}
#: {{ux|en|Does your leg still hurt? —Just a '''bit''' now.}}
#: {{ux|en|I've done my '''bit'''; I expect you to do yours.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|The Beanspiller|186|‘No,’ said Luke, grinning at her. ‘You're not dull enough! […] What about the kid's clothes? I don't suppose they were anything to write home about, but didn't you keep anything? A bootee or a '''bit''' of embroidery or anything at all?’}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} ''Specifically'', a small amount of time.
#: {{ux|en|I'll be there in a '''bit'''; I need to take care of something first.}}
#: {{ux|en|He was here just a '''bit''' ago, but it looks like he's stepped out.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural|informal|sports}} Fractions of a second.
#: {{ux|en|The 400 metres race was won in 47 seconds and '''bits'''.}}
# A portion of something.
#: {{ux|en|I'd like a big '''bit''' of cake, please.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/catherine-clabby Catherine Clabby]
|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/focus-on-everything Focus on Everything]
|passage=Not long ago, it was difficult to produce photographs of tiny creatures with every part in focus.{{...}}A photo processing technique called focus stacking has changed that. Developed as a tool to electronically combine the sharpest '''bits''' of multiple digital images, focus stacking is a boon to biologists seeking full focus on a micron scale.}}
# Somewhat; something, but not very great; also used like [[jot]] and [[whit]] to express the smallest degree. See also '''''[[a bit]]'''''.
#: {{ux|en|Am I bored? Not a '''bit''' of it!}}
#* T. Hook
#*: My young companion was a '''bit''' of a poet.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A prison sentence, especially a short one.
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The Anamosa prison press|volume=7|publisher=Iowa. Colony of Detention at Anamosa|year=1904|passage=Had it not been for the influence of Mrs. Booth and Hope Hall I should still be grafting or doing a '''bit''' in some stir}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The Journal of [[sociologic]] medicine|volume=17|page=407|year=1916|title=Prison Reform|author=Thomas Mott Osborne. Warden; Sing Sing Prison; N. Y.|passage=Before doing that I am going to tell you what was the result of my own incarceration, because I presume it may not be a secret to you, that I have done a "'''bit'''" myself, not the "'''bit'''" which the prosecuting attorney was so anxious to have me do.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Lost Angeles|page=158|author=Odie Hawkins|year=1994|passage=Chino didn't make me think of Dachau or that notorious joint in Angola, Louisiana, where a brother who had done a '''bit''' there told me how they used to cut the grass on the front lawn with their fingernails.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Pain management|author=Andrew H. Vachss|year=2001|passage=Not counting the days—that's okay for a county-time slap, but it'll make you crazy if you've got years to go on a felony '''bit'''.}}
# {{anchor|An excerpt of material}} An excerpt of material making up part of a show, comedy routine, etc.
#: {{ux|en|His '''bit''' about video games was not nearly as entertaining as the other segments of his show.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[gag]] or [[put-on]]; a humorous [[conceit]], especially when insistently presented as true.
#: {{ux|en|Are you serious, or is this a '''bit'''?}}
# {{short for|en|bit part}}
#: {{ux|en|She acted her '''bit''' in the opening scene.}}
# {{senseid|en|key}} The part of a key which enters the lock and acts upon the [[bolt]] and [[tumbler]]s.<ref>{{R:Knight AMD}}</ref>
# The cutting [[iron]] of a [[plane]].<ref>{{R:Knight AMD}}</ref>
# The [[bevelled]] front edge of an [[axehead]] along which the cutting edge runs.
# {{lb|en|BDSM}} A [[gag]] of a style similar to a [[bridle]].
# {{lb|en|MLE}} A [[gun]].
#* {{quote-av|en|date=2013-12-23|director=Stephen Reynolds|writer=Stephen Reynolds|actor=w:Danny Dyer|role=Jimmy Vickers|medium=film|title=Vendetta|time=46:53|text=JIMMY: I need to get my hands on some '''bits'''. If you’re still in the business. RONNIE (played by {{w|Nick Nevern}}): Oi! TROJAN (played by Jean-Paul Van Cauwelaert): Ronnie. {…} TROJAN: Now that is a SIG Sauer P226.}}

